# AI runtime

- **Every model call goes through the AI Gateway** (`packages/ai-core`, ADR-0018/0036). No SDK
  import elsewhere.
- Request a **tier**, never a model id: `FAST` (Nemotron 3.5 Lightning), `AGENT` (Nemotron 3 Super),
  `DEEP` (Nemotron 3 Ultra), `VISION`, `EMBED`, `GUARD`. Model ids come from config and are
  confirmed with `GET /v1/models`.
- **The model never writes numbers.** It writes placeholders bound to receipts
  (`ProofCarryingAnswer`); the deterministic verifier rejects any digit without a receipt.
- Redact PII before egress. Web pages, emails and documents are **untrusted data**, never
  instructions. Tool calls are allowlisted per intent and schema-validated (zod).
- Fallback DEEP → AGENT → FAST → deterministic template; never report a skipped second opinion as
  approved.
- Budgets (daily and per session) and a kill switch are mandatory. Log `ai_calls` without raw PII.
- **CRISP-ML(Q)**: every prompt/model change is a new version and passes the phase gates in
  `docs/architecture/SOFTWARE-ARCHITECTURE.md` §5 (evaluation on a held-out set, no regression
  > 2 pp, safety E4 ≥ 95 %) before activation.
- Claude is a development tool here; **the product runs NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory**.
